From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: power: supply: add the references for direct charging

A UPM6720 can charge directly from a PPS source. It needs the port and
the fuel gauge for that, and its limits are written at probe once they
are there, which a 9 V contract needs as well: from reset its input FETs
open above 6.5 V.

The MT6375 charger decides when that happens, so it needs to know the
charge pump.

---
 .../power/supply/mediatek,mt6375-charger.yaml     |  7 +++++++
 .../bindings/power/supply/nuvolta,nu2115.yaml     | 15 +++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/mediatek,mt6375-charger.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/mediatek,mt6375-charger.yaml
index 4eba260..1df598d 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/mediatek,mt6375-charger.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/mediatek,mt6375-charger.yaml
@@ -39,6 +39,13 @@ properties:
       The power supply of the USB port controller, which tells how much current
       the port can give. Without it the input stays at the USB default.
 
+  mediatek,charge-pump:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
+    description:
+      A charge pump to charge through directly from a PPS source, within the
+      limits of this charger's policy. Used only when the direct_charge module
+      parameter is on.
+
   mediatek,connector-thermal-zone:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/string
     description:
diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/nuvolta,nu2115.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/nuvolta,nu2115.yaml
index 8537e7c..d81b502 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/nuvolta,nu2115.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/nuvolta,nu2115.yaml
@@ -33,10 +33,25 @@ properties:
     description: The FETs at the VAC1 input, closed by hand.
     unevaluatedProperties: false
 
+  unisemi,usb-port:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
+    description:
+      The USB Type-C port controller whose power supply gives PPS. With this
+      and unisemi,fuel-gauge a UPM6720 charges directly when its main charger
+      asks for it, and its limits are written at probe.
+
+  unisemi,fuel-gauge:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
+    description: The fuel gauge of the battery behind the charge pump.
+
 required:
   - compatible
   - reg
 
+dependencies:
+  unisemi,usb-port: [ "unisemi,fuel-gauge" ]
+  unisemi,fuel-gauge: [ "unisemi,usb-port" ]
+
 additionalProperties: false
 
 examples:
